        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Reluctance to reduce staff headcount",
          "block_bbox": [
            110,
            1913,
            1085,
            1980
          ],
          "block_id": 6,
          "block_order": 7,
          "group_id": 6,
          "block_polygon_points": [
            [
              110.0,
              1913.0
            ],
            [
              1085.0,
              1913.0
            ],
            [
              1085.0,
              1980.0
            ],
            [
              110.0,
              1980.0
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "Leaders are reluctant to include job reductions in cost-cutting measures, but some have been forced to reduce headcount, tenured status and salary costs to lower expenditure. Other approaches to reducing payroll include cutting non-teaching staff through hiring freezes, replacing leavers with more junior staff and merging roles.",
          "block_bbox": [
            104,
            2026,
            1432,
            2292
          ],
          "block_id": 7,
          "block_order": 8,
          "group_id": 7,
          "block_polygon_points": [
            [
              104.0,
              2026.0
            ],
            [
              1432.0,
              2026.0
            ],
            [
              1432.0,
              2292.0
            ],
            [
              104.0,
              2292.0
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "However, these initiatives will only get institutions so far. Some universities are thinking more strategically about their workforce strategies to prevent over-hiring, using data to predict demand and hire accordingly.",
          "block_bbox": [
            104,
            2332,
            1430,
            2498
          ],
          "block_id": 8,
          "block_order": 9,
          "group_id": 8,
          "block_polygon_points": [
            [
              104.0,
              2332.0
            ],
            [
              1430.0,
              2332.0
            ],
            [
              1430.0,
              2498.0
            ],
            [
              104.0,
              2498.0
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "block_label": "text",
          "block_content": "While headcount reductions save money in the short term, leaders are apprehensive about the longer-term costs associated with these measures. Some noted the cultural cost of redundancies, with a loss of morale as remaining staff fear for the safety of their jobs. One Vice Chancellor in Australia said that reducing staff numbers inevitably removed staff who had just been trained or upskilled, creating zero return on this investment. Leaders are also concerned that reducing headcount could erode the capacity of staff to engage in essential transformation projects.\nWe invest a lot of money and time in developing people, so to get rid of them only to re-hire them in 12 months doesn't make sense.",
          "block_bbox": [
            105,
            2537,
            1428,
            2960
          ],
          "block_id": 9,
          "block_order": 10,
          "group_id": 9,
